1
00:01:31,508 --> 00:01:40,948
Hina was anxious with a lot on her mind.

2
00:01:48,468 --> 00:01:50,688
Why not fried chicken and rolled omelette?

3
00:01:50,788 --> 00:01:51,768
What do you think of that?

4
00:01:52,028 --> 00:01:54,148
And what about sweet and salty kinkura?

5
00:01:54,348 --> 00:01:56,288
No! Nothing brown!

6
00:01:56,788 --> 00:01:58,408
It has to be a cute luncheon!

7
00:01:58,488 --> 00:01:59,428
Brown is not cute!

8
00:01:59,868 --> 00:02:01,448
Maybe you can't understand.

9
00:02:02,068 --> 00:02:03,608
It has to be like...

10
00:02:03,608 --> 00:02:04,248
Ta-da!

11
00:02:04,768 --> 00:02:05,568
Then he'll be a...

12
00:02:05,568 --> 00:02:06,428
Wow, how cute!

13
00:02:07,908 --> 00:02:10,228
But he's a middle school boy, isn't he?

14
00:02:10,468 --> 00:02:13,148
Don't you think he might be more interested in...

15
00:02:13,148 --> 00:02:15,668
Something that's delicious looking rather than cute?

16
00:02:16,128 --> 00:02:17,348
What do you think, Ray?

17
00:02:17,628 --> 00:02:18,868
How'd you peel so many?

18
00:02:19,288 --> 00:02:20,708
You did that really fast!

19
00:02:21,308 --> 00:02:22,268
Oh, yeah.

20
00:02:23,888 --> 00:02:25,068
Tomorrow is Sunday.

21
00:02:26,468 --> 00:02:27,828
You're so precise.

22
00:02:28,188 --> 00:02:29,828
You're really good with your hands.

23
00:02:30,028 --> 00:02:31,168
I'm glad you came over.

24
00:02:31,168 --> 00:02:33,088
I have over eight pounds of these.

25
00:02:33,568 --> 00:02:36,628
The baseball team from Hina's middle school will be having a game.

26
00:02:37,728 --> 00:02:40,468
You know, I've never tried eating chestnuts before.

27
00:02:40,888 --> 00:02:41,888
They look kind of interesting.

28
00:02:42,308 --> 00:02:43,848
I wonder if there's something I'd like.

29
00:02:44,148 --> 00:02:44,588
Definitely.

30
00:02:44,888 --> 00:02:46,328
It's the perfect winter snack.

31
00:02:46,828 --> 00:02:49,568
And if you boil it down to a pulp, it lasts a long time.

32
00:02:50,108 --> 00:02:51,708
Hina has a crush on one of the players.

33
00:02:52,248 --> 00:02:54,548
She's going to his game tomorrow to cheer him on.

34
00:02:54,548 --> 00:02:57,168
Takahashi's the son of a milkman.

35
00:02:57,168 --> 00:02:59,428
He's pretty tall for a boy his age.

36
00:02:59,768 --> 00:03:02,668
He must have grown up drinking lots of milk as a boy.

37
00:03:03,048 --> 00:03:03,588
It's funny.

38
00:03:03,808 --> 00:03:06,108
He used to be shorter than Hina back in grade school.

39
00:03:07,048 --> 00:03:11,888
But now, he's an ace baseball player and very popular at Hina's school.

40
00:03:12,248 --> 00:03:16,328
Hina's been putting a lot of effort into making Takahashi a perfect homemade lunch.

41
00:03:16,708 --> 00:03:19,688
It's a big event, and everything has to be just right.

42
00:03:19,888 --> 00:03:21,908
Guess you've got more competition now.

43
00:03:22,268 --> 00:03:25,968
You've liked Takahashi since elementary school, but I guess you're not the only one.

44
00:03:26,548 --> 00:03:27,868
I don't like him!

45
00:03:28,068 --> 00:03:29,128
It's not like that!

46
00:03:29,268 --> 00:03:31,468
Why do you always have to try and make it all romantic?

47
00:03:31,848 --> 00:03:32,968
Stop being stupid!

48
00:03:33,388 --> 00:03:35,368
Sorry, didn't mean to upset you.

49
00:03:35,948 --> 00:03:38,688
It's the night before the big day that she's been waiting for.

50
00:03:38,988 --> 00:03:40,628
And I'm here to witness it.

51
00:03:41,468 --> 00:03:44,468
All while peeling the chestnuts that are ready to be boiled.

52
00:03:44,468 --> 00:03:50,148
What do you think about this stuff?

53
00:03:50,448 --> 00:03:51,268
Think about what?

54
00:03:51,448 --> 00:03:52,068
Let me see.

55
00:03:52,988 --> 00:03:57,168
You want to make pumpkin croquettes shaped like apples in a flower bed made of rice balls?

56
00:03:58,148 --> 00:04:02,888
Boil and mash the pumpkin, cover it with flour, then cut with egg yolk and breadcrumbs.

57
00:04:03,808 --> 00:04:04,448
Let's see.

58
00:04:04,748 --> 00:04:06,208
The game starts at 10, right?

59
00:04:06,708 --> 00:04:11,328
If you leave the house at 9.30, that's cutting it pretty close for the first time making all of this.

60
00:04:11,628 --> 00:04:13,888
You may need more time, and that'll make you nervous.

61
00:04:13,888 --> 00:04:17,668
And the more you rush around in the kitchen, the more likely you'll make mistakes.

62
00:04:18,008 --> 00:04:20,208
Well, what exactly do you think I should do?

63
00:04:20,468 --> 00:04:21,168
Keep it simple.

64
00:04:21,508 --> 00:04:22,868
Fried chicken and rolled omelet.

65
00:04:23,288 --> 00:04:25,288
You could add some color with a cherry tomato.

66
00:04:26,568 --> 00:04:28,688
But is there anything I can eat now?

67
00:04:29,348 --> 00:04:30,908
I don't want to make any of that!

68
00:04:31,008 --> 00:04:32,228
It's like old lady food!

69
00:04:32,428 --> 00:04:33,508
Just forget it!

70
00:04:33,948 --> 00:04:34,348
God!

71
00:04:34,348 --> 00:04:35,968
Oh, lady!

72
00:04:36,328 --> 00:04:37,148
Never mind!

73
00:04:37,268 --> 00:04:38,448
I'll figure it out myself!

74
00:04:38,808 --> 00:04:39,468
Fine then!

75
00:04:39,568 --> 00:04:40,968
Just go ahead and do what you want!

76
00:04:41,068 --> 00:04:42,308
I'm done giving you advice!

77
00:04:42,428 --> 00:04:43,628
It's not like you're listening anyway!

78
00:04:43,628 --> 00:04:44,128
Don't, don't!

79
00:04:44,128 --> 00:04:50,688
No way!

80
00:04:50,748 --> 00:04:51,568
It's already 9!

81
00:04:51,708 --> 00:04:53,628
I think the supermarket's open till 10!

82
00:04:54,308 --> 00:04:56,308
I have no more money!

83
00:04:56,308 --> 00:05:07,748
So, um, hey sis, I want to buy all these ingredients, but I don't have enough money for it, so, um...

84
00:05:07,748 --> 00:05:09,908
Let's take a look.

85
00:05:10,408 --> 00:05:18,308
Winter squash, ground beef, breadcrumbs, onions, eggs, black pepper, radishes, olives, avocado, asparagus, baby corn, balsamic vinegar, lemons, red and yellow...

86
00:05:18,308 --> 00:05:19,068
Make some more!

87
00:05:19,248 --> 00:05:19,968
Why did you stop?

88
00:05:19,968 --> 00:05:20,168
Make some more!

89
00:05:20,168 --> 00:05:20,248
Make some more!

90
00:05:20,248 --> 00:05:21,228
Why did you stop?

91
00:05:21,228 --> 00:05:23,668
How much are you planning on making?

92
00:05:24,048 --> 00:05:25,788
And how much were you gonna spend?

93
00:05:26,168 --> 00:05:27,548
This isn't cost effective!

94
00:05:27,988 --> 00:05:30,268
This will cost over 3,000 yen!

95
00:05:30,628 --> 00:05:31,868
We don't have that kind of money!

96
00:05:32,248 --> 00:05:36,448
We can't spend 3,000 yen of our own budget just to buy some other kid's lunch!

97
00:05:36,628 --> 00:05:41,208
The only time we splurge on milk for ourselves is when it's on sale for 158 yen!

98
00:05:41,548 --> 00:05:41,848
No!

99
00:05:42,808 --> 00:05:43,728
Excuse me?

100
00:05:43,908 --> 00:05:44,788
Some other kid?

101
00:05:44,968 --> 00:05:46,308
But what about the cats and Ray?

102
00:05:46,388 --> 00:05:47,208
Aren't they the same?

103
00:05:47,208 --> 00:05:47,628
Huh!

104
00:05:47,628 --> 00:05:49,868
What the heck?

105
00:05:49,988 --> 00:05:52,488
Why didn't you get to use our money on people outside the family?

106
00:05:52,928 --> 00:05:54,488
You're not part of my family?

107
00:05:55,848 --> 00:05:59,148
How come you're not Momo's big brother?

108
00:05:59,908 --> 00:06:01,628
Uh, well, I...

109
00:06:02,388 --> 00:06:03,208
I'm sorry.

110
00:06:03,308 --> 00:06:03,868
Help!

111
00:06:04,808 --> 00:06:05,988
This is awkward.

112
00:06:08,568 --> 00:06:09,628
Um, so...

113
00:06:10,228 --> 00:06:11,508
I'm sorry.

114
00:06:12,168 --> 00:06:13,548
No, I'm the one who's sorry.

115
00:06:14,108 --> 00:06:16,408
I offered to pay for my share of food before.

116
00:06:16,408 --> 00:06:19,148
It's just that Akari would never accept my money.

117
00:06:19,708 --> 00:06:22,708
Maybe after what happened tonight, she'll change her mind and let me pay.

118
00:06:23,268 --> 00:06:25,828
Then I guess I wouldn't feel so guilty whenever I come over.

119
00:06:26,188 --> 00:06:26,588
Ah!

120
00:06:26,648 --> 00:06:26,848
Ah!

121
00:06:27,088 --> 00:06:27,288
Ah!

122
00:06:27,288 --> 00:06:32,888
Akari has a soft spot for all kinds of strays.

123
00:06:33,448 --> 00:06:34,608
Dogs and cats.

124
00:06:35,088 --> 00:06:35,908
Anything really.

125
00:06:36,348 --> 00:06:38,508
When she sees scrawny strays, she feels bad.

126
00:06:39,288 --> 00:06:42,868
She takes care of them, till they're soft and fluffy again.

127
00:06:42,868 --> 00:06:47,648
But I was surprised when I found out she actually brought a person home one day.

128
00:06:48,168 --> 00:06:48,748
Who, me?

129
00:06:49,188 --> 00:06:50,448
But I don't mind, really.

130
00:06:50,828 --> 00:06:52,468
She'll make you soft and fluffy, too.

131
00:06:52,808 --> 00:06:54,348
She just needs a little more time.

132
00:06:55,068 --> 00:06:56,268
Yeah, you think so?

133
00:06:56,908 --> 00:06:57,208
Hmm.

134
00:06:57,208 --> 00:06:59,168
I see.

135
00:06:59,808 --> 00:07:00,128
Yep.

136
00:07:00,568 --> 00:07:01,208
You'll see.

137
00:07:01,208 --> 00:07:28,208
So on Sunday morning...

138
00:07:28,208 --> 00:07:33,048
I spent so much time making these!

139
00:07:33,228 --> 00:07:34,508
I gotta start all over!

140
00:07:36,168 --> 00:07:36,968
Something's burning!

141
00:07:38,268 --> 00:07:39,148
Apple saute!

142
00:07:39,288 --> 00:07:39,868
It's a fire!

143
00:07:44,748 --> 00:07:45,868
Sloppy, sloppy!

144
00:07:46,128 --> 00:07:46,868
What time is it?

145
00:07:48,608 --> 00:07:50,008
Ain't already you know!

146
00:07:50,428 --> 00:07:52,208
But I woke up at six o'clock!

147
00:07:52,208 --> 00:07:55,188
Who could be calling at this hour?

148
00:07:55,368 --> 00:07:55,888
I'm busy!

149
00:07:58,748 --> 00:07:59,628
Where's Yoko?

150
00:08:01,168 --> 00:08:03,088
I'm running a little late.

151
00:08:03,248 --> 00:08:04,328
Just leave without me.

152
00:08:04,568 --> 00:08:04,768
There.

153
00:08:05,148 --> 00:08:06,148
What should I wear?

154
00:08:06,908 --> 00:08:10,548
I was so focused on lunch that I didn't even think about what I should wear!

155
00:08:11,888 --> 00:08:13,228
Maybe this is too flashy.

156
00:08:13,748 --> 00:08:15,728
Does this make me look desperate for his attention?

157
00:08:17,808 --> 00:08:19,768
How'd it get so late so fast?

158
00:08:19,768 --> 00:08:32,648
Curtains are more expensive than I thought.

159
00:08:33,288 --> 00:08:35,628
But now I'll finally be able to sleep in later.

160
00:08:36,228 --> 00:08:38,308
I don't have any matches coming up for a while.

161
00:08:38,748 --> 00:08:42,208
So this is a good opportunity to get everything that I need for the apartment.

162
00:08:42,208 --> 00:08:45,728
I still need a chair, a desk, a bookshelf.

163
00:08:47,208 --> 00:08:47,388
Huh?

164
00:08:49,448 --> 00:08:51,848
Oh, they're having a game at Hina's middle school.

165
00:08:58,488 --> 00:09:01,108
Oh, it's the famous Takahashi.

166
00:09:01,648 --> 00:09:02,648
He's huge!

167
00:09:02,948 --> 00:09:04,668
I can't believe he's only in middle school.

168
00:09:05,108 --> 00:09:06,708
He seems like a pretty cool guy, though.

169
00:09:06,708 --> 00:09:10,908
There's Hina.

170
00:09:11,288 --> 00:09:12,128
She looks excited.

171
00:09:12,708 --> 00:09:14,228
I wonder if she made his luncheon time.

172
00:09:14,468 --> 00:09:15,288
Let's go!

173
00:09:15,708 --> 00:09:15,928
Huh?

174
00:09:16,168 --> 00:09:16,748
Whoa!

175
00:09:18,088 --> 00:09:19,308
It's a slowback!

176
00:09:20,488 --> 00:09:20,968
Takahashi!

177
00:09:21,608 --> 00:09:22,988
A home run?

178
00:09:27,988 --> 00:09:28,588
Takahashi!

179
00:09:28,708 --> 00:09:29,488
You're welcome!

180
00:09:30,268 --> 00:09:31,708
You're welcome, Takahashi!

181
00:09:31,928 --> 00:09:32,488
Yay!

182
00:09:32,488 --> 00:09:34,608
He did it all right!

183
00:09:34,788 --> 00:09:35,948
That was so cool.

184
00:09:36,468 --> 00:09:37,688
He knocked it out of the park.

185
00:09:40,228 --> 00:09:44,308
He totally looks like the main character from some boy's manga.

186
00:09:45,268 --> 00:09:47,588
I've never seen Hina act like this before.

187
00:09:48,268 --> 00:09:50,488
She is clearly smitten with this guy.

188
00:09:51,328 --> 00:09:52,468
This is real for her.

189
00:09:52,788 --> 00:09:54,468
I think she could be falling in love.

190
00:09:56,908 --> 00:09:57,428
Love.

191
00:10:02,488 --> 00:10:20,228
Thank you.

192
00:10:22,228 --> 00:10:24,468
After getting dressed, we're heading to Matsuda.

193
00:10:24,968 --> 00:10:25,908
Ah, Matsuda?

194
00:10:26,148 --> 00:10:26,648
For Monja?

195
00:10:26,908 --> 00:10:27,788
Sounds great!

196
00:10:28,348 --> 00:10:29,488
Is Takahashi around?

197
00:10:29,668 --> 00:10:30,608
Coming, Takahashi?

198
00:10:30,608 --> 00:10:31,528
To Matsuda?

199
00:10:32,308 --> 00:10:33,228
Ah, thanks.

200
00:10:35,288 --> 00:10:35,728
Takahashi?

201
00:10:36,328 --> 00:10:37,068
Are you all right?

202
00:10:37,148 --> 00:10:37,848
Sounds great!

203
00:10:37,948 --> 00:10:38,708
Can we go too?

204
00:10:38,848 --> 00:10:39,468
All right!

205
00:10:39,588 --> 00:10:40,388
Moja it is!

206
00:10:43,668 --> 00:10:45,008
So what should I get?

207
00:10:45,408 --> 00:10:46,508
Come on, Takahashi!

208
00:10:46,588 --> 00:10:47,028
Let's go!

209
00:10:47,028 --> 00:11:15,088
Don't do it.

210
00:11:15,088 --> 00:11:19,228
But what will Akari say about this?

211
00:11:19,908 --> 00:11:22,088
She's gonna ask me why I didn't give it to him.

212
00:11:22,448 --> 00:11:24,808
She'll say after all that trouble, why didn't you?

213
00:11:25,168 --> 00:11:25,688
What?

214
00:11:26,188 --> 00:11:29,488
She'll never understand what it was like for me today.

215
00:11:29,928 --> 00:11:31,208
Why is she crying?

216
00:11:32,368 --> 00:11:34,488
I mean, she's naturally beautiful.

217
00:11:34,948 --> 00:11:37,048
And she's always been a good cook.

218
00:11:37,048 --> 00:11:42,588
So anyone, I'd be happy to have lunch made by her.

219
00:11:43,528 --> 00:11:47,188
She looked so happy last night, and even earlier today.

220
00:11:48,028 --> 00:11:49,048
But now...

221
00:11:49,048 --> 00:11:57,408
All right now, let's go home.

222
00:11:57,508 --> 00:11:58,128
We'll eat it there.

223
00:11:58,128 --> 00:12:02,288
I guess...

224
00:12:02,288 --> 00:12:04,088
I just don't understand girls.

225
00:12:08,488 --> 00:12:09,708
Welcome home!

226
00:12:09,708 --> 00:12:23,488
I see.

227
00:12:23,928 --> 00:12:25,648
You weren't able to give it to him.

228
00:12:26,068 --> 00:12:27,208
Well, that's too bad.

229
00:12:27,208 --> 00:12:30,928
Well, you certainly did your best.

230
00:12:36,688 --> 00:12:37,888
Oh, there, there.

231
00:12:37,948 --> 00:12:38,788
It'll be all right.

232
00:12:39,068 --> 00:12:40,048
I know how you feel.

233
00:12:40,568 --> 00:12:42,708
The exact same thing happened to me before.

234
00:12:43,048 --> 00:12:43,868
I understand.

235
00:12:43,868 --> 00:12:48,248
You weren't able to give someone you liked the lunch you made?

236
00:12:49,768 --> 00:12:51,168
I was just like you.

237
00:12:51,368 --> 00:12:52,888
I didn't have the courage to do it.

238
00:12:53,328 --> 00:12:55,768
I wanted to make the perfect cute lunch so badly.

239
00:12:56,548 --> 00:12:58,888
I think my nerves got to me, and then I failed.

240
00:13:00,728 --> 00:13:02,808
That's why I couldn't help saying what I did.

241
00:13:03,828 --> 00:13:06,208
But later, I remembered something.

242
00:13:06,948 --> 00:13:08,908
You know what I said to you yesterday evening?

243
00:13:09,508 --> 00:13:12,508
It's the same thing that mom had told me when I was your age.

244
00:13:12,508 --> 00:13:16,588
I guess you could say, like mother, like daughter.

245
00:13:17,888 --> 00:13:19,008
Isn't that funny?

246
00:13:20,068 --> 00:13:21,548
Mom said that to you?

247
00:13:24,668 --> 00:13:27,508
So, let's see how it turned out.

248
00:13:30,628 --> 00:13:31,148
Yeah.

249
00:13:36,428 --> 00:13:38,248
What? You want some?

250
00:13:39,688 --> 00:13:41,148
Well, just this once.

251
00:13:41,148 --> 00:13:42,788
Really? I get to have some?

252
00:13:44,548 --> 00:13:46,528
Okay, the tea's finally ready.

253
00:13:47,108 --> 00:13:47,768
Let's eat.

254
00:13:48,848 --> 00:13:50,228
What happened to the kitties?

255
00:13:50,728 --> 00:13:53,568
Looks to me like they ate themselves into a food coma.

256
00:13:55,028 --> 00:13:56,528
So, how is it?

257
00:13:59,868 --> 00:14:02,468
Hina, did you taste this while making it?

258
00:14:02,468 --> 00:14:08,788
It had a bitter taste to it, while also being sweet and sour.

259
00:14:09,328 --> 00:14:12,528
All the flavors you're left with at the end of a first love.

260
00:14:13,688 --> 00:14:16,008
Next time, let me help you in the kitchen.

261
00:14:17,208 --> 00:14:18,968
I'll give it my best shot!

262
00:14:19,488 --> 00:14:23,408
Maybe it's a good thing she wasn't able to give him her first homemade lunch.

263
00:14:23,408 --> 00:14:26,488
At least, that's what Rei and I thought.

264
00:14:26,988 --> 00:14:29,048
She still has a long way to go.

265
00:14:29,048 --> 00:14:40,268
I can see it!

266
00:14:41,348 --> 00:14:41,748
What?

267
00:14:42,548 --> 00:14:44,708
Uh, you know I'm the one who won, right?

268
00:14:44,948 --> 00:14:45,228
Hmm?

269
00:14:45,668 --> 00:14:47,088
Yeah, I guess you could say that.

270
00:14:47,188 --> 00:14:48,408
But it was just an anomaly.

271
00:14:48,928 --> 00:14:51,608
Mmm, it's not an anomaly if it happens all the time.

272
00:14:53,968 --> 00:14:55,288
Ah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

273
00:14:55,588 --> 00:14:57,548
If you say so, you won, okay?

274
00:14:57,688 --> 00:14:59,968
Jeez, whatever makes you feel better about it.

275
00:15:00,108 --> 00:15:01,008
Hey, wait a minute.

276
00:15:01,228 --> 00:15:02,288
What are you trying to pull here?

277
00:15:02,348 --> 00:15:05,328
Being all, fine, if you say so, doesn't change anything.

278
00:15:05,808 --> 00:15:08,308
Okay, one more game and I'll go first.

279
00:15:08,588 --> 00:15:11,788
I'll start off with the static rook and you do the bishop exchange once more.

280
00:15:11,788 --> 00:15:13,008
Huh? What the heck?

281
00:15:13,068 --> 00:15:14,948
It's like you're using me as a practice board.

282
00:15:15,108 --> 00:15:15,688
That's it!

283
00:15:16,108 --> 00:15:17,228
You're being petty!

284
00:15:17,228 --> 00:15:19,108
This requires expediency.

285
00:15:19,608 --> 00:15:22,168
We can't allow the bishop exchange to rule the board.

286
00:15:22,308 --> 00:15:24,028
We have to find something that can stop it.

287
00:15:24,348 --> 00:15:24,748
Huh?

288
00:15:25,048 --> 00:15:27,388
If you want to win, you should use the ranging rook.

289
00:15:27,508 --> 00:15:29,328
But I like using the static rook!

290
00:15:30,448 --> 00:15:33,408
You won't even let me practice the move I'm still not good at.

291
00:15:34,308 --> 00:15:35,548
Eh, whatever.

292
00:15:35,988 --> 00:15:39,708
How many times do I have to tell you that I would prefer to study by myself?

293
00:15:40,008 --> 00:15:41,868
We raise each other up, you and I.

294
00:15:42,148 --> 00:15:45,728
You'd be losing out on a very important part of your shogi life without our rivalry!

295
00:15:45,728 --> 00:15:48,028
You understand that, don't you?

296
00:15:48,728 --> 00:15:49,328
Kiriyama!

297
00:15:49,668 --> 00:15:53,088
Time is of the essence and the two of us need to find it!

298
00:15:53,308 --> 00:15:54,948
We can't waste a single moment!

299
00:15:55,408 --> 00:15:58,168
In fact, you have to be the one that discovers it!

300
00:15:58,548 --> 00:16:01,108
The bishop exchange crusher silver bullet.

301
00:16:01,648 --> 00:16:02,148
Yes!

302
00:16:02,148 --> 00:16:04,588
It's the Nikaido vaccine!

303
00:16:04,908 --> 00:16:05,308
Huh?

304
00:16:05,888 --> 00:16:08,568
If I discover it, it'll be the Kiriyama vaccine!

305
00:16:09,308 --> 00:16:11,148
But it's what I've been dreaming of!

306
00:16:11,528 --> 00:16:13,028
The Nikaido vaccine!

307
00:16:13,248 --> 00:16:14,688
Or the Nikaido system!

308
00:16:15,028 --> 00:16:17,708
I want to leave behind a technique with my name on it!

309
00:16:17,948 --> 00:16:18,848
Don't you understand?

310
00:16:18,848 --> 00:16:20,408
I understand it?

311
00:16:20,608 --> 00:16:22,168
That doesn't mean I agree with it!

312
00:16:22,708 --> 00:16:23,688
Good morning!

313
00:16:24,428 --> 00:16:29,468
You suddenly showed up at 9 in the morning saying something about developing a silver bullet technique.

314
00:16:29,808 --> 00:16:33,648
And besides, I'm an all-rounder, so I'm not interested in that kind of...

315
00:16:33,648 --> 00:16:35,168
Hey, is this getting through to you?

316
00:16:38,888 --> 00:16:41,048
Okay, let's get some lunch.

317
00:16:41,048 --> 00:16:44,408
Where to?

318
00:16:44,988 --> 00:16:46,188
Let's get some fast food.

319
00:16:46,528 --> 00:16:48,048
Oh yeah, how about Mech Burger?

320
00:16:48,468 --> 00:16:49,628
Have you tried the Giga Mech?

321
00:16:49,848 --> 00:16:50,788
You'd probably like it.

322
00:16:50,988 --> 00:16:52,268
The Giga Mech?

323
00:16:55,808 --> 00:16:56,668
We'll pass.

324
00:16:57,228 --> 00:16:59,728
So what do you usually wind up getting for lunch?

325
00:17:00,008 --> 00:17:00,608
Oh, me?

326
00:17:01,248 --> 00:17:04,828
Well, when I'm alone, I guess I usually get a burger or a beef bowl.

327
00:17:05,268 --> 00:17:06,748
It just kind of depends on how I feel.

328
00:17:06,748 --> 00:17:11,288
But lately, I've been having dinner at my friend's house whenever I can.

329
00:17:13,488 --> 00:17:14,708
Is that you, Momo?

330
00:17:16,828 --> 00:17:17,608
What's wrong?

331
00:17:17,788 --> 00:17:18,628
Where are your sisters?

332
00:17:24,528 --> 00:17:25,048
Bado!

333
00:17:27,208 --> 00:17:27,728
Bado!

334
00:17:28,728 --> 00:17:29,068
Huh?

335
00:17:29,968 --> 00:17:31,628
Kiriyama, do you know this little girl?

336
00:17:32,208 --> 00:17:33,408
Uh, well, yeah.

337
00:17:33,408 --> 00:17:38,308
If I'm not mistaken, it sounded like she yelled Botoro right before she jumped on me.

338
00:17:38,768 --> 00:17:40,488
You know who Botoro is, don't you?

339
00:17:40,608 --> 00:17:44,008
It's an anime masterpiece loved by children, adults, and yours truly.

340
00:17:44,268 --> 00:17:48,588
It's a story about a big, intelligent creature that lives in a beautiful, magical forest.

341
00:17:48,748 --> 00:17:49,308
Bado!

342
00:17:49,368 --> 00:17:49,708
Awesome!

343
00:17:50,208 --> 00:17:54,168
I admit, I do feel a deep connection to Botoro since we're both so bright.

344
00:17:55,068 --> 00:17:56,368
All right, little girl.

345
00:17:56,568 --> 00:17:57,328
Who are you?

346
00:17:57,688 --> 00:17:58,628
What's your name?

347
00:17:59,428 --> 00:17:59,908
Momo!

348
00:18:00,528 --> 00:18:01,708
All right then, Momo.

349
00:18:01,968 --> 00:18:03,248
Let's all walk together.

350
00:18:03,688 --> 00:18:06,348
The traffic is dangerous here, so we should hold hands.

351
00:18:10,208 --> 00:18:12,928
Momo looks much happier with him than she does with me.

352
00:18:13,248 --> 00:18:16,128
I'll see to it personally that we get you safely home.

353
00:18:16,348 --> 00:18:17,488
Oh, there she is!

354
00:18:17,628 --> 00:18:17,888
Momo!

355
00:18:18,308 --> 00:18:19,988
Hey, it looks like she found Rei!

356
00:18:20,228 --> 00:18:22,128
Hi, thanks for taking care of Momo!

357
00:18:23,608 --> 00:18:24,368
Hi, Rei.

358
00:18:24,568 --> 00:18:26,448
So, um, who was your friend?

359
00:18:26,448 --> 00:18:26,948
Oh, no way!

360
00:18:26,948 --> 00:18:30,128
Not you too, Akari.

361
00:18:30,368 --> 00:18:31,728
Her face is all flushed.

362
00:18:31,908 --> 00:18:33,968
Don't tell me she has a weakness for him too!

363
00:18:35,568 --> 00:18:36,368
That guy?

364
00:18:37,008 --> 00:18:39,128
Um, well, you see, he's from Shogi.

365
00:18:39,568 --> 00:18:40,748
I mean, my club!

366
00:18:41,748 --> 00:18:42,748
Nice to meet you.

367
00:18:43,088 --> 00:18:44,928
My name is Harunobu Nikaido.

368
00:18:45,168 --> 00:18:47,048
I'm Rei's best friend and rival.

369
00:18:48,808 --> 00:18:50,168
Have you two eaten yet?

370
00:18:50,388 --> 00:18:52,548
You're both welcome to join us for dinner if you'd like.

371
00:18:52,888 --> 00:18:54,028
Another outsider?

372
00:18:54,688 --> 00:18:56,088
Well, how very kind of you.

373
00:18:56,348 --> 00:18:57,808
Yes, it would be my pleasure.

374
00:18:57,808 --> 00:19:06,068
Come on, Boudou!

375
00:19:06,528 --> 00:19:07,948
Let's vote some more!

376
00:19:12,448 --> 00:19:14,048
This house is old.

377
00:19:15,588 --> 00:19:18,228
It looks like a vintage movie set.

378
00:19:20,008 --> 00:19:22,328
I'm really sorry about my sister.

379
00:19:22,988 --> 00:19:23,608
It's okay.

380
00:19:23,728 --> 00:19:25,488
You don't have anything to apologize for.

381
00:19:26,188 --> 00:19:27,248
Chico, Chico!

382
00:19:28,808 --> 00:19:29,328
Chubby!

383
00:19:30,148 --> 00:19:31,268
Chubby, Chubby!

384
00:19:32,388 --> 00:19:34,028
How do I explain it?

385
00:19:34,528 --> 00:19:37,428
Your friend is just like a strong and vibrant ball!

386
00:19:38,628 --> 00:19:39,868
Wait, like a ball?

387
00:19:40,148 --> 00:19:42,988
I don't think I've ever heard anyone describe a friend like that.

388
00:19:43,008 --> 00:19:46,248
I'm sorry, but Akari's pretty fond of soft and fluffy things.

389
00:19:46,608 --> 00:19:47,708
She can't help herself.

390
00:19:50,088 --> 00:19:51,588
Which would you prefer to have?

391
00:19:51,948 --> 00:19:55,328
We went grocery shopping today so I can make pretty much anything you'd like.

392
00:19:55,328 --> 00:19:57,648
Some fried chicken or maybe a steak?

393
00:19:57,808 --> 00:20:01,528
Fried chick?

394
00:20:02,528 --> 00:20:05,648
I'd rather have something that's bland and light on protein.

395
00:20:06,268 --> 00:20:07,848
I mean, that's okay.

396
00:20:07,928 --> 00:20:08,408
I'm sorry.

397
00:20:08,588 --> 00:20:09,028
Never mind.

398
00:20:09,328 --> 00:20:10,068
Anything's fine.

399
00:20:10,708 --> 00:20:11,488
You can choose.

400
00:20:11,488 --> 00:20:13,588
Oh, if you insist.

401
00:20:14,068 --> 00:20:14,768
That's unusual.

402
00:20:15,208 --> 00:20:16,888
I guess you have a pretty mature palate.

403
00:20:17,368 --> 00:20:17,948
That's odd.

404
00:20:18,208 --> 00:20:21,048
How can he maintain such a plump physique if that's all he eats?

405
00:20:21,448 --> 00:20:22,668
Maybe he's on a diet!

406
00:20:23,048 --> 00:20:23,548
Oh no!

407
00:20:23,788 --> 00:20:25,788
Then he'll lose that round and shapely form!

408
00:20:25,788 --> 00:20:26,748
I understand.

409
00:20:26,948 --> 00:20:29,248
It probably bothers him to be so big at his age.

410
00:20:29,548 --> 00:20:30,388
A slow metabolism.

411
00:20:30,888 --> 00:20:33,228
What if the situation's even more serious?

412
00:20:33,708 --> 00:20:33,988
No.

413
00:20:34,368 --> 00:20:38,408
No matter how wonderfully soft he is, it doesn't mean a thing unless he's healthy.

414
00:20:38,828 --> 00:20:39,468
It's okay.

415
00:20:39,708 --> 00:20:40,768
Leave your health to me.

416
00:20:40,768 --> 00:20:42,228
It's so delicious.

417
00:20:42,768 --> 00:20:44,568
Sorry for troubling you, Ikari.

418
00:20:44,808 --> 00:20:46,608
I promised you wouldn't say that, remember?

419
00:20:47,248 --> 00:20:48,828
Life's too hard, Ikari.

420
00:20:49,228 --> 00:20:51,488
I can't have any melanin or bamboo shoes.

421
00:20:51,888 --> 00:20:53,808
I just don't know what I can eat anymore.

422
00:20:53,948 --> 00:20:55,948
I can't even enjoy booze like before.

423
00:20:56,208 --> 00:20:57,688
Doc says I can only have a little.

424
00:20:58,068 --> 00:20:59,408
Poor Mr. Yamamoto.

425
00:20:59,488 --> 00:21:00,248
That's awful.

426
00:21:00,568 --> 00:21:01,488
I'll see if I can find some mild...

427
00:21:01,488 --> 00:21:07,008
I didn't take care of my granny or listen to my customers complain about their dietary restrictions for nothing!

428
00:21:11,088 --> 00:21:12,048
There you are.

429
00:21:12,348 --> 00:21:15,128
Season it however you like to suit your taste, Saranobu.

430
00:21:17,268 --> 00:21:17,748
Delicious!

431
00:21:18,208 --> 00:21:19,628
Even though it's kind of bland.

432
00:21:19,788 --> 00:21:21,468
I'm so glad you like it.

433
00:21:21,768 --> 00:21:23,388
Chew well and eat slowly, okay?

434
00:21:26,268 --> 00:21:26,748
Right.

435
00:21:26,848 --> 00:21:30,908
My butler always tells me I should slow down and chew each bite at least 30 times.

436
00:21:30,908 --> 00:21:32,848
Except I find I'm always too impatient.

437
00:21:33,188 --> 00:21:35,708
Well, I guess you're lucky he cares that much.

438
00:21:40,528 --> 00:21:41,008
Huh?

439
00:21:41,148 --> 00:21:43,388
Who could be visiting us at this hour of the night?

440
00:21:46,648 --> 00:21:48,828
Terribly sorry to disturb you this evening.

441
00:21:50,468 --> 00:21:53,668
It looks like the young master has been enjoying your hospitality.

442
00:21:54,228 --> 00:21:55,208
Hey, Hanaoka!

443
00:21:55,528 --> 00:21:56,968
Did you come here to pick me up?

444
00:21:57,008 --> 00:21:58,728
So you're Harunobu's butler.

445
00:21:58,728 --> 00:22:00,868
I'm surprised you were able to find us.

446
00:22:00,908 --> 00:22:01,848
It wasn't hard.

447
00:22:01,848 --> 00:22:03,268
I just used a GPS.

448
00:22:05,348 --> 00:22:06,348
Oh, excuse me.

449
00:22:06,348 --> 00:22:08,248
I may have a touch of bronchitis.

450
00:22:08,248 --> 00:22:10,688
Nevertheless, I just happened to be passing by.

451
00:22:10,688 --> 00:22:14,948
He always manages to pick me up no matter where I am and never fails to find me.

452
00:22:14,948 --> 00:22:16,768
Guess it's always been like that.

453
00:22:16,768 --> 00:22:18,068
Just like magic.

454
00:22:18,068 --> 00:22:19,188
Magic?

455
00:22:19,188 --> 00:22:20,528
Wait a second, Nikaido.

456
00:22:20,528 --> 00:22:22,488
Don't you know you're under total surveillance?

457
00:22:22,488 --> 00:22:23,988
He just said GPS.

458
00:22:23,988 --> 00:22:25,928
I know that's what he just said.

459
00:22:25,928 --> 00:22:29,268
So if you'd like, please enjoy these treats, everyone.

460
00:22:29,268 --> 00:22:32,708
They're from a local confectionery shop you may have already heard about.

461
00:22:32,708 --> 00:22:34,268
They're my personal favorite.

462
00:22:34,268 --> 00:22:35,708
Please enjoy some.

463
00:22:35,708 --> 00:22:36,708
How nice.

464
00:22:36,708 --> 00:22:37,648
Thanks so much.

465
00:22:37,648 --> 00:22:38,648
Oh my.

466
00:22:38,648 --> 00:22:39,648
What a coincidence.

467
00:22:39,648 --> 00:22:41,648
These are my favorite cakes as well.

468
00:22:41,648 --> 00:22:43,648
How lovely.

469
00:22:43,648 --> 00:22:46,648
Please come in and join us if you'd like.

470
00:22:46,648 --> 00:22:48,648
I'll put on some tea, alright?

471
00:22:48,648 --> 00:22:50,648
Oh, don't mind if I do.

472
00:22:50,648 --> 00:22:51,648
Thank you.

473
00:22:51,648 --> 00:22:53,648
I'm so glad you can join us.

474
00:22:53,648 --> 00:22:55,648
Hina, would you boil some water?

475
00:22:55,648 --> 00:22:56,648
Okay.

476
00:24:31,011 --> 00:24:36,011
He was a close friend of my dad's.

477
00:24:38,011 --> 00:24:42,011
Even though he was an adult, he always treated me with respect.

478
00:24:43,011 --> 00:24:47,011
Tell me, Ray, do you want to play more Shogi?

479
00:24:47,011 --> 00:24:49,011
What's wrong?

480
00:24:51,011 --> 00:24:54,011
Watch the next episode of March Comes In Like A Lion!

481
00:24:54,011 --> 00:24:58,011
I swear, I won't mess up the next lunch I make!

482
00:25:01,011 --> 00:25:07,011
Book 3

483
00:25:07,011 --> 00:25:10,011
I can't eat that섯, but he asked me her to do.

484
00:25:10,011 --> 00:25:12,011
Wow!

485
00:25:14,011 --> 00:25:17,011
She was in love, thank you and God.

486
00:25:18,011 --> 00:25:22,071
Xi, Hallelujah!

487
00:25:23,071 --> 00:25:27,571
Look, you've moved her!

